<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Holiday returns one week after starting buprenorphine with naloxone and is seen by Dr. Ortiz of addiction medicine on the same day. She took half a film on the first day and one film daily since, under the tongue each morning, without missing a dose. She has used no heroin or other opioids. She had no withdrawal, but cravings come back each evening, most of all after a show. She has had mild constipation and no drowsiness. She picked up two naloxone two-packs; her friend came with her and was shown how to use them. She is still drinking four or five drinks on performance nights. She read her results from last week by phone. She says she came back because nobody lectured her at the first visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Buprenorphine</td><td>8 mg daily for six days, every dose taken</td></tr><tr><td>Opioid use</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Cravings</td><td>Every evening, strongest after shows</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Mild constipation</td></tr><tr><td>Naloxone</td><td>Two two-packs dispensed; her friend trained</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Four or five drinks on performance nights</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

